  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_07eb96ef40fb41c48dcbbe27159b12d3",
      "statement": "The in-process bus fans events to subscribers with a 1024-event buffer each; Publish is non-blocking and a full subscriber is dropped (removed and its channel closed) so Publish never blocks; a dropped subscriber ends its SSE connection and the client reconnects.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/bus/bus.go#L10-L65",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3ab07d26718cb35891fdd86a5ba1878b403bfa575156d52bd8108e64e5bfd996:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_986c2ede1525446298976a74349610b5",
      "statement": "The server SSE handler streams bus events as data: {json} newline-newline frames flushed per event (with text/event-stream, no-cache, X-Accel-Buffering: no headers); the frame is written as three separate writes to avoid fmt buffer growth; a failed write ends the response so the client reconnects, and a bus-closed channel (subscriber overflow) also ends the stream.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/server/sse.go#L9-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:267c9c23b54475f46e6bfc2f475a2e05c423dd10290cfde68a2bf3200c0d7db5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5bd13256e23740f39b5de3bab6994356",
      "statement": "The TUI SSE client reconnects with backoff on every dropped /event connection and pings a resync channel per drop; because the bus has no replay, events published in the gap are unrecoverable and the caller must re-hydrate state over REST on each ping; reconnects must never be silent (a silent reconnect previously left the footer stuck on busy).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/tui/client/event.go#L19-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e611f9006ebd45cf072bcb7972a38d0993e10512607acdffd9d1292836104ae7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9c9abb0594f4464396a63b4644114cda",
      "statement": "The SSE scanner token buffer is capped at 4 MiB because a single data: line carries one whole event JSON and escaped tool output exceeded the former 1 MiB cap; scanner overflow still aborts the stream and fires the resync ping, bounded by the re-hydrate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/tui/client/event.go#L71-L99",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:77f69f8a3ce7649b0dd76a33d4d55b1e27b0eb217173a5656438ff64e85a0679:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_665f3befdada405eb2370af30c9de236",
      "statement": "The TUI eventPump blocks on the SSE channel and delivers each event as EventMsg, re-arming itself on every event; on channel close it delivers connLostMsg and stops.",
